  "limits": [
    "Immutable plan metadata and fingerprints are durable; complete reviewed input payloads and historical release provenance are not yet persisted/resolved by a formal entry point.",
    "Caller-provided release fingerprint and retirement evidence fingerprint do not authenticate artifacts or prove an old process has stopped. Trusted management authorization and evidence collection remain required.",
    "The dictionary adapter covers exactly registry retirement and dictionary adoption. It does not provision identities, approve dictionaries/resources, publish configuration or establish whole-platform readiness.",
    "RECONCILE_ONLY uncertain work cannot be blindly replayed; generic cancellation/compensation is not implemented. Domain adapters must truthfully implement durable idempotency before automatic retry is allowed.",
    "No runtime RPC/HTTP installation methods, actual network deployment, production configuration/data changes, commit or push.",
    "Credential lifecycle, caller policies, MQ ACL, configuration/process rollout, other legacy adoption, remaining module entrances, formal one-JVM standalone and three-topology full business verification remain unfinished."
  ]
